<title>UK: Ventspils crude pipeline closes, Novorossiisk open.</title>
<headline>Ventspils crude pipeline closes, Novorossiisk open.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A crude oil pipeline feeding the Latvian Baltic port of Ventspils closed early on Friday for unscheduled maintenance work, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The line, which carries Russian Urals crude, shut at 0911 local time on Friday for minor repairs.</p>
<p>&quot;They're promising it will be back up again this evening,&quot; said the source.</p>
<p>Meanwhile in the Black Sea, the key Russian port of Novorossiisk was open again after high winds forced a suspension of berthings on Wednesday and Thursday.</p>
<p>Two crude tankers were alongside and three were at anchor, waiting to berth, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
